  "comments": "In 1985 the Royal Mint released the second one pound coin in the &#039;Royal Diadem&#039; series, the first with the Maklouf third portrait of HM The Queen. The coin was issued as part of the 1985 Annual Coin Sets in both Brilliant Uncirculated (178,375 sales) &amp; Proof versions as well as individually in a BU pack (24,850 sales).<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5ed13910ca6ce.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5ed13910ca6ce.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"191\" height=\"250\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/608882a065d4f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/608882a065d4f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"129\" height=\"249\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThis Leslie Durbin reverse design was repeated one more time on a second edition in 1990, again issued as part of the 1990 Annual Coin Sets in both Brilliant Uncirculated &amp; Proof versions.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5ed139711be0e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5ed139711be0e.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"224\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThe coin was also struck in silver proof and silver piedfort.",
